        "results_interpretation": "The pooled analysis of seven studies examining the association between choline intake and breast cancer incidence yielded an effect size of 0.78, indicating a potential inverse relationship. However, the 95% confidence interval of (0.59, 1.04) spans the null value, suggesting that the data do not support a statistically significant association between choline and breast cancer. Furthermore, the high heterogeneity, indicated by an I\u00b2 of 83.97%, highlights considerable variability among the studies, which may complicate the interpretation of the pooled results. Overall, these findings suggest that choline is not associated with breast cancer incidence, warranting further investigation into the role of this nutrient across diverse populations and study designs."
